WEBVTT

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:02.299
It takes 150 flowers to make one

00:00:02.319 --> 00:00:03.607
gram of this spice.

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.661
Course one begins in a field at

00:00:05.681 --> 00:00:06.307
dawn.

00:00:06.668 --> 00:00:08.587
One gram of saffron takes about one

00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:10.324
hundred and fifty flowers.

00:00:10.854 --> 00:00:12.575
Each flower blooms for only a few

00:00:12.595 --> 00:00:14.839
days a year, and holds just three

00:00:14.859 --> 00:00:16.066
crimson threads.

00:00:16.427 --> 00:00:17.963
Every thread is picked by hand,

00:00:17.983 --> 00:00:19.595
before the sun can fade it.

00:00:20.125 --> 00:00:22.133
The threads are slowly dried,

00:00:22.157 --> 00:00:24.652
until deep red turns to liquid gold.

00:00:25.106 --> 00:00:26.289
Did you already know?

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.046
That is why saffron is the most

00:00:28.066 --> 00:00:29.702
expensive spice on Earth.

00:00:30.232 --> 00:00:31.118
Back in the kitchen,

00:00:31.138 --> 00:00:32.604
the chef soaks the threads in warm

00:00:32.624 --> 00:00:33.180
milk.

00:00:33.541 --> 00:00:35.785
Good to know: this releases the color

00:00:35.805 --> 00:00:37.689
and flavor, so a pinch can paint

00:00:37.709 --> 00:00:39.113
a whole pot of rice.

00:00:39.643 --> 00:00:41.569
Worth the price or a total rip-off?

00:00:41.744 --> 00:00:43.183
Drop your take below.
